      "correctAnswer": "Use direct mode for the variable rename (well-understood, straightforward) and use the explore subagent for the WebSocket investigation (open-ended, requires investigation before action).\n\nThe key distinction is ambiguity, not difficulty. The variable rename is well-understood with a clear action \u2014 direct mode is appropriate. The WebSocket issue is open-ended and requires investigation before any action can be taken \u2014 the explore subagent is designed for this kind of investigative work. Option A wastes time planning a simple rename. Option C is wrong because jumping to direct implementation on an intermittent distributed systems issue without investigation is premature. Option D reverses the logic \u2014 planning a simple rename is unnecessary, and directly implementing a fix for an uninvestigated issue is risky.",
