      "correctAnswer": "Identify the 200 failed requests by their custom_id and resubmit only those failed requests in a new batch.\n\nThe Batches API assigns each request a custom_id, which allows teams to identify exactly which requests failed and resubmit only those in a new batch. This avoids reprocessing the 4,800 successful requests and maintains cost efficiency. Option A wastes resources by reprocessing requests that already succeeded. Option C is incorrect \u2014 the Batches API does not automatically retry failed requests. Option D is unnecessarily expensive; the Batches API handles resubmissions the same as initial submissions, and switching to synchronous processing forfeits the 50% cost savings.",
