      "correctAnswer": "Structurally reorder the input so that the most critical sections appear at the beginning and end of the context.\n\nThis describes the lost-in-the-middle effect, where models underperform on findings located in the middle of long inputs. The fix is structural reorder of the input, not prompt reminders. Option A is explicitly wrong \u2014 prompt reminders do not fix the lost-in-the-middle effect. Option C, while splitting can help, merging without deduplication introduces new problems and does not address the structural ordering principle. Option D is incorrect because temperature controls sampling randomness, not positional attention.",
