      "explanation": "The agent should never use heuristic selection for ambiguous customer matching. It must ask the customer for additional identifiers to disambiguate.\n\nFor ambiguous customer matching, the correct approach is to ask for additional identifiers \u2014 never heuristic selection. Selecting based on fuzzy matching risks acting on the wrong customer record. Option A is wrong because no heuristic threshold makes automatic selection acceptable in ambiguous identity scenarios. Option C is wrong because ambiguity in matching is not a policy violation (which would be a documented \"no\"); it is a resolvable situation that the agent can handle by requesting more information. Option D is wrong because proceeding with ambiguous identity creates downstream risk and violates proper identity verification practices."
