      "explanation": "Structured error context including: the failure type (database unavailability), the attempted query, the partial results from successful sources, and alternative approaches \u2014 plus coverage annotations noting which findings are well-supported and where gaps exist.\n\nThe correct approach combines structured error context (failure type, attempted query, partial results, alternative approaches) with coverage annotations that note which findings are well-supported versus where gaps exist. This enables the orchestrator and downstream agents to make informed decisions. Option A is the silent suppression anti-pattern \u2014 omitting the failure prevents any recovery or awareness of gaps. Option C is the workflow termination anti-pattern \u2014 killing the entire pipeline over a single partial failure. Option D is impractical and introduces unbounded latency; the system should proceed with annotated partial results."
