      "explanation": "This approach follows the principle of **Data Normalization at the Middleware Layer**. LLMs are reasoning engines, not\nreliable data processors or format converters; asking an LLM to handle mixed data types (Unix vs. ISO) invites\nhallucinations and logic errors. By implementing a normalization hook or wrapper, you intercept the raw tool output and\ntransform it into a unified format (typically ISO 8601) *before* it enters the agent's context window. This ensures the\nmodel receives a clean, consistent data structure, effectively eliminating the risk of misinterpretation caused by\nformat heterogeneity."
