      "explanation": "This workflow follows the **Map-Reduce** architectural pattern for LLM task processing.\n\n1. **The \"Map\" Phase:** By processing each ticket individually, you ensure the model allocates its full context window\n   and \"attention\" to every single record. This prevents the \"lost in the middle\" phenomenon, where LLMs degrade in\n   performance when analyzing large, multi-item lists in a single prompt. It also allows you to extract consistent,\n   structured metadata (e.g., JSON logs) for every ticket.\n2. **The \"Reduce\" Phase:** The synthesis agent then consumes the *structured output* of the first 50 runs. This is\n   significantly more efficient and accurate than asking the model to \"remember\" the nuances long, unstructured\n   conversations. The synthesis agent can perform statistical reasoning, clustering, and trend analysis on the clean\n   data generated by the first pass."
