      "explanation": "This approach applies the **Single Responsibility Principle** to tool design. LLMs are optimized to match a user's\nintent to a specific tool schema. When you provide a \"God-tool\" (a single, monolithic function handling disparate\ntasks), you drastically increase the dimensionality of the parameter space. The model must parse one massive schema to\ndetermine *which* parameters apply to *which* sub-operation.\n\nBy splitting the tool, you:\n\n1. **Reduce Parameter Hallucination:** Each tool schema only contains the parameters relevant to that specific task. The\n   model no longer sees \"password\" parameters when it is trying to \"change subscription.\"\n2. **Simplify Selection:** The model chooses the tool based on the action, not based on an arbitrary string enum\n   parameter.\n3. **Improve Type Safety:** Each tool can have a strictly defined JSON schema, allowing for native validation at the\n   API/MCP gateway level before the request is even passed to the tool implementation."
