      "explanation": "Autonomous agents rely on high-fidelity feedback to perform recursive planning. A generic \"Operation failed\" provides\nzero semantic information, forcing the agent to guess the nature of the failure. This creates two distinct operational\nfailures:\n\n1. **The Retry Loop (Transient Error Failure):** If the agent treats a policy violation (terminal) as a timeout (\n   recoverable), it may enter an infinite retry loop, wasting computational resources and increasing latency.\n2. **The Policy Blind Spot (Semantic Error Failure):** If the agent treats a timeout (recoverable) as a policy\n   violation (terminal), it may erroneously report to the customer that their item is \"non-returnable\" when the system\n   was actually just overloaded. This destroys customer trust and leads to false customer service outcomes."
