      "explanation": "This configuration leverages **Context-Aware Rule Scoping**. By utilizing YAML frontmatter (also known as \"rule\nfrontmatter\"), you instruct Claude Code to index and activate specific rules only when the file path matches the defined\npattern.\n\n* **Precision:** The agent will not load these rules into its context window when editing `src/utils/math.ts` (a\n  non-test file), preserving context capacity for more relevant instructions.\n* **Automation:** By placing this in `claude/rules/` and committing to the repository, the scoping applies universally\n  across the team, removing the need for manual configuration or environment-specific setup.\n* **Scalability:** This approach decouples file-specific logic from global rules. You can maintain separate, highly\n  specific rule files for different file types (e.g., `rules/tests.md`, `rules/api.md`, `rules/security.md`) without\n  them clashing or bloating the context window."
