      "question": "The agent has access to `process_refund`. Stakeholders are concerned about the \"rogue agent\" scenario where the model\ncalls the tool on the wrong order due to a hallucination. How do you implement a \"Human-in-the-Loop\" (HITL) for this\nspecific tool?\n\n* Configure the MCP server to require a manual API key input for every refund.\n* Add a `requires_approval: true` flag to the tool definition in the MCP server, and handle the logic in the client to\n  pause the agent and request human confirmation.\n* Tell the model: \"Please ask a human before calling `process_refund`.\"\n* Remove the `process_refund` tool and have the model write the refund details to a file for a human to process later.",
