      "explanation": "The primary criteria for escalation in an agentic workflow are **Policy Ambiguity** and **Business Judgment**.\n\n* **Policy Interpretation vs. Policy Execution:** An AI agent excels at *execution* (applying a clear rule: \"If X and Y,\n  then Z\"). It fails at *interpretation* (deciding if a new, undocumented business scenario warrants a deviation from\n  standard practice).\n* **The \"Silent Policy\" Trap:** When policy is silent, the agent has no deterministic path. Allowing the agent to \"\n  guess\" or formulate a response on behalf of the company carries financial and reputational risk. Escalation to a human\n  is the only way to establish a precedent in a novel, ambiguous situation."
