      "correctAnswer": "The asynchronous model prevents executing tools mid-request and returning results for Claude to continue analysis.\n",
      "explanation": "Batch processing APIs are architected for **high-throughput, one-shot inference** where the model completes the entire\nrequest without external intervention or intermediate state changes.\n\n* **Synchronous vs. Asynchronous Loops:** The tool-calling workflow you described requires a **stateful, interactive\n  loop**. The model must (1) receive input, (2) emit a tool call, (3) stop generation, (4) allow the environment to\n  execute the tool, and (5) feed the result back to the model for the next turn.\n* **Batch Execution Incompatibility:** Batch APIs are inherently asynchronous and \"blind\" to external feedback loops.\n  Once a batch task is submitted, it is computed in an offline, isolated environment. There is no mechanism to pause the\n  model generation, inject tool outputs, and resume the generation within the same batch inference job."
