      "question": "You have two review modes: a pre-merge-commit hook (blocking) and \"deep analysis\" (runs overnight). You want to use the\nMessage Batches API (50% savings, 24-hour latency). Which mode should use batch processing?\n\n* A) Pre-merge-commit hook only\n* **B) Deep analysis only**\n* C) Both modes\n* D) Neither mode",
      "correctAnswer": "Deep analysis only.",
      "explanation": "The choice depends entirely on the **latency requirements of the execution path**.\n\n* **Pre-merge-commit hooks** are synchronous bottlenecks. They exist to block the PR merge process until specific\n  criteria are met. If a developer pushes code and must wait up to 24 hours for a \"batch\" result, the development\n  velocity drops to zero. This creates a severe negative impact on Developer Experience (DX).\n* **Deep analysis** is an asynchronous, background process. Since it already runs overnight and is designed to handle \"\n  polling\" for completion, the latency of the Batch API is transparent to the user. It is the ideal candidate for cost\n  optimization because it provides high value (detailed suggestions) without needing immediate, real-time availability."
