      "correctAnswer": "It arbitrarily averages two different metrics from different sources without acknowledging the methodological\ndifferences.\n\nThe sources report different metrics (installed capacity vs. generation output) using different methodologies.\nArbitrarily averaging them into a single figure misrepresents both sources. The correct approach is to preserve both\nvalues with source attribution and explain the methodological difference, letting readers understand the distinction\nbetween capacity and generation measurements.",
