      "correctAnswer": "Expose the endpoint catalog as an MCP resource so Claude can see available data without exploratory tool calls.\n\nMCP resources are a mechanism for exposing content catalogs (e.g., API endpoints, documentation hierarchies, database\nschemas) to give agents visibility into available data without requiring exploratory tool calls. If the resource is\nproperly exposed but not being used, enhancing the resource description to explain what it contains and when to use it\nwould help.",
      "explanation": "Expose the endpoint catalog as an MCP resource so Claude can see available data without exploratory tool calls.\n\nMCP resources are a mechanism for exposing content catalogs (e.g., API endpoints, documentation hierarchies, database\nschemas) to give agents visibility into available data without requiring exploratory tool calls. If the resource is\nproperly exposed but not being used, enhancing the resource description to explain what it contains and when to use it\nwould help."
