      "question": "Your extraction pipeline uses Pydantic for output validation. Sometimes validation fails due to type mismatches\u2014dates in\nunexpected formats, numbers as strings, etc.\n\n**What is the correct retry-with-feedback approach?**\n\n- **A.** Send a follow-up request including the original document, the failed extraction, and the specific validation\n  error for model self-correction.\n- **B.** Simply retry the same extraction request hoping for better results.\n- **C.** Skip validation for fields that frequently fail and accept the raw output.\n- **D.** Pre-process all documents to normalize formats before extraction.",
      "correctAnswer": "Send a follow-up request including the original document, the failed extraction, and the specific validation\nerror for model self-correction.\n\nThe retry-with-error-feedback pattern involves appending specific validation errors to the prompt on retry to guide the\nmodel toward correction. Simply retrying without feedback wastes tokens, and skipping validation undermines data\nquality. Pre-processing can help but doesn't address the core issue of format variation.",
      "explanation": "Send a follow-up request including the original document, the failed extraction, and the specific validation\nerror for model self-correction.\n\nThe retry-with-error-feedback pattern involves appending specific validation errors to the prompt on retry to guide the\nmodel toward correction. Simply retrying without feedback wastes tokens, and skipping validation undermines data\nquality. Pre-processing can help but doesn't address the core issue of format variation."
