      "question": "PDF parsing frequently encounters failures (corrupted sections, password protection). Currently, these terminate the subagent and trigger coordinator intervention.\n\n**What's the most effective architectural improvement to reduce coordinator involvement in routine error handling?**\n\n- **A.** Create a dedicated error-handling agent\n- **B.** Have the coordinator validate all documents before dispatching\n- **C.** Configure subagents to always return partial results with \"success\" status\n- **D.** Have the subagent implement local recovery for transient failures and only propagate errors it cannot resolve to the coordinator",
