      "question": "The agent is handling a refund request. The `get_customer` tool returns multiple matches for the customer name provided. Currently, the agent selects the customer with the most recent order, but this causes errors in 15% of multi-match cases.\n\n**How should you address this?**\n\n- **A.** Modify `get_customer` to return only the single most likely match\n- **B.** Implement a confidence scoring system to rank matches\n- **C.** Instruct Claude to ask for an additional identifier (email, phone, or order number) when `get_customer` returns multiple matches\n- **D.** Add few-shot examples of using conversational context to disambiguate",
      "correctAnswer": "Instruct Claude to ask for an additional identifier when multiple matches are returned.\n\nRequesting a unique identifier from the user is the most reliable way to disambiguate `get_customer` results. While this adds a conversational turn, it eliminates the error rate caused by the model attempting to guess between valid matches.",
      "explanation": "Instruct Claude to ask for an additional identifier when multiple matches are returned.\n\nRequesting a unique identifier from the user is the most reliable way to disambiguate `get_customer` results. While this adds a conversational turn, it eliminates the error rate caused by the model attempting to guess between valid matches."
