      "question": "For simple requests, the agent has a 91% resolution rate. For complex requests (e.g., \"I've been charged twice and I want to cancel\"), the agent takes 12+ tool calls with only a 54% resolution rate, often investigating concerns sequentially.\n\n**What is the most effective change?**\n\n- **A.** Decompose the request into distinct concerns, then investigate each in parallel using shared customer context before synthesizing a resolution\n- **B.** Add explicit verification gates between steps\n- **C.** Consolidate tools into a single `investigate_issue` tool\n- **D.** Add few-shot examples of sequences",
      "correctAnswer": "Decompose the request into distinct concerns and investigate in parallel.\n\nRequest decomposition and parallel investigation address efficiency bottlenecks. This approach reduces the number of tool calls by preventing slow sequential steps and avoids redundant data fetching, allowing the agent to synthesize a unified resolution more reliably than a massive `investigate_issue` tool.",
      "explanation": "Decompose the request into distinct concerns and investigate in parallel.\n\nRequest decomposition and parallel investigation address efficiency bottlenecks. This approach reduces the number of tool calls by preventing slow sequential steps and avoids redundant data fetching, allowing the agent to synthesize a unified resolution more reliably than a massive `investigate_issue` tool."
