      "question": "The team implements an incremental review strategy: Claude Code reviews only the changed files in a PR rather than the entire codebase. However, a reviewer notices that Claude Code sometimes misses issues that depend on understanding unchanged code (e.g., a changed function call where the function definition was not modified).\n\n**How should the team address this?**\n\n- **A.** Always send the entire codebase to Claude Code to ensure full context\n- **B.** Provide the changed files as the primary review target, but also include relevant context files (e.g., imported modules, type definitions, function signatures referenced by the changed code) so Claude Code has enough context to understand cross-file dependencies without reviewing the entire codebase\n- **C.** Ignore cross-file issues \u2014 they will be caught by unit tests\n- **D.** Run two separate reviews \u2014 one for changed files and one for the entire codebase \u2014 and merge findings",
