      "correctAnswer": "The `tool_use` approach.\n\nThe `tool_use` mechanism is more reliable for structured extraction because it enforces the parameter schema at the API level. When Claude calls a tool, the arguments must conform to the tool's defined parameter schema, guaranteeing valid JSON with the expected structure. Free-text JSON (A) can have formatting issues, missing fields, or extra content. Regex parsing (C) is fragile. Schema complexity (D) does not determine which approach is better \u2014 tool_use handles complex nested schemas well.",
