      "correctAnswer": "Return structured error context to the coordinator including the failure type, the attempted query, any partial\nresults, and potential alternative approaches.",
      "explanation": "Intelligent recovery requires that the coordinator receive sufficient information to select among available recovery\npaths. A structured error payload \u2014 failure type, attempted query, partial results, alternative approaches \u2014 gives the\ncoordinator the full decision surface: it can retry the same query, reformulate the query, substitute an alternative\nsource, proceed with partial results, or escalate based on task priority. Each piece of context eliminates a class of\nrecovery errors. Without structured context, the coordinator is forced to make recovery decisions from a position of\ninformation deficit, producing recovery actions that are generic rather than calibrated to the specific failure."
