      "question": "The document analysis agent encounters two credible sources with conflicting statistics (40% vs. 12% growth) on a key\nresearch metric. The discrepancy is significant and impacts the validity of the research conclusions. What is the most\neffective way for the document analysis agent to handle this conflict?\n\n* Apply source credibility heuristics to select the most likely accurate figure, complete the analysis using that value,\n  and include a footnote mentioning the discrepancy.\n* **Complete the document analysis with both figures included, explicitly annotate the conflict with source attribution,\n  and let the coordinator decide how to reconcile before passing to synthesis.**\n* Halt analysis and escalate to the coordinator immediately, asking it to determine which source is authoritative before\n  the agent continues processing remaining documents.\n* Include both figures in the analysis output without flagging them as conflicting, allowing the synthesis agent to\n  determine which to use based on the broader research context.",
      "correctAnswer": "Complete the document analysis with both figures included, explicitly annotate the conflict with source attribution,\nand let the coordinator decide how to reconcile before passing to synthesis.",
