      "question": "The synthesis agent frequently needs to verify specific claims. Currently, it returns control to the coordinator, which\ninvokes the web search agent, then re-invokes synthesis. This creates 2-3 round trips per task, increasing latency by\n40%. 85% of these verifications are simple fact-checks, while 15% require deeper investigation. What's the most\neffective approach to reduce overhead while maintaining reliability?\n\n* **A) Give the synthesis agent a scoped `verify_fact` tool for simple lookups, while complex verifications continue\n  delegating to the web search agent through the coordinator.**\n* B) Give the synthesis agent access to all web search tools so it can handle any verification need directly.\n* C) Have the web search agent proactively cache extra context around each source during initial research.\n* D) Have the synthesis agent accumulate all verification needs and return them as a batch to the coordinator at the end\n  of its pass.",
